00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.930
JOE: Children on the autism spectrum
are more likely to have a restricted

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.280
diet, eating a more limited
range or refusing more foods than

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.970
their typically developing peers.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.689
BETH: A child with autism can
be helped to be distracted from

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.400
their anxiety overeating, by
stimulating their other senses.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:23.020
Making them feel relaxed can help,
by making sure their seat is comfy

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.890
and maybe playing some music or
a story to keep them relaxed.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:31.689
JOE: Individuals who find food smells
overpowering, may prefer to eat bland

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.049
food whilst those who have an under
sensitivity to smell and taste, may

00:00:36.049 --> 00:00:40.490
prefer stronger flavours and some strong
smells may be a source of pleasure.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:46.459
Some people find hard food or sloppy
food unbearable, while others may be

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.060
supersensitive to the texture of food
and have to touch everything with

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.359
their fingers to see how it feels
before putting it in their mouth.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.089
BETH: Modifying food to improve
the sensory experience, such as

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:02.560
puréeing, and introducing a new
food or textures in small steps, can

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.610
help with gradual desensitisation.

00:01:06.179 --> 00:01:10.220
To introduce a new food a series
of small steps can be tried.

00:01:10.879 --> 00:01:16.300
The individual should be able to just look
at it, touch it, put it on their plate,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:24.270
then smell it, lick it, put it into their
mouth, bite it, chew it, and swallow it.

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:28.259
If they don’t like it, they may
spit it out, but this should

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.689
not be looked at negatively, as
it might not happen next time.

00:01:32.569 --> 00:01:36.580
This can go on potentially for
months until an individual gets more

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.550
comfortable with the new sensations.

